{"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "A Blog article in SinglePageStartup has several identities: a database record, an SDK result, a selected frontend variant and a place in a saved page composition. Keeping those identities explicit makes a visual change easier to review. The article can acquire a new card layout while its ID, localized content, linked files and business operations remain the same. Start with the owning Blog component and follow its reader before changing the surrounding page."}]}, {"type": "heading", "attrs": {"level": 2}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Follow the saved record"}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The Article default variant demonstrates the normal SPS arrangement. Its index.tsx binds the Blog client SDK, server SDK, Provider, loading component and visual component to the shared default component. Component.tsx renders the loaded record. This arrangement gives record loading a clear owner. Adding another fetch inside the visual component would create a second request and a second loading lifecycle for the same entity."}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The public discriminator belongs in interface.ts. Its literal value must also appear in the effective variants registry and props union. A folder containing JSX is insufficient if a saved variant cannot select it. The root registry combines the singlepage and startup layers; an override must replace the matching implementation and its public contract together. This matters when a project adds required props to an inherited variant."}]}, {"type": "heading", "attrs": {"level": 2}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Choose the execution side"}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Next.js Server Components and Client Components have different execution capabilities. The "}, {"type": "text", "text": "Next.js 15 documentation", "marks": [{"type": "link", "attrs": {"href": "https://nextjs.org/docs/15/app/getting-started/server-and-client-components", "target": "_blank", "rel": "noopener noreferrer nofollow"}}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " describes serializable props and composition through children. SPS applies that boundary inside its component template: index.tsx chooses execution, readers obtain data, and an interactive ClientComponent owns hooks and browser state. The isServer prop selects SPS reading behavior; a real client JSX boundary still needs an appropriate client entrypoint."}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "An ordinary saved-record view uses the shared reader. A custom operation can justify local client.tsx and server.tsx readers, with the same typed result supplied to Component.tsx. Those files replace the relevant reading behavior. Wrapping the unchanged shared reader inside another Provider would give ownership to both. Keep the specialized SDK operation visible in the public request and result types so a reviewer can verify what the view actually loads."}]}, {"type": "heading", "attrs": {"level": 2}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Pass loaded records explicitly"}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "When a parent already has the current SDK result, dataSource="props" lets a child render it without fetching again. The parent retains query subscriptions, loading and error state. A later refetch supplies new props. A constant query function returning an old record would keep that record detached from subsequent reconciliation."}]}, {"type": "codeBlock", "attrs": {"language": "tsx"}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "<Article
  variant="overview-default"
  isServer={props.isServer}
  dataSource="props"
  data={props.data}
  language={props.language}
>
  {props.children}
</Article>"}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "This is the composition used by the Blog overview wrapper. At a server-to-client boundary, pass only the UI inputs the child declares. A broad props spread can carry SDK bindings, Providers or constructors from the reader. A TypeScript cast does not turn those values into serializable data. Resolve server render callbacks on the server and pass their rendered React nodes to client slots."}]}, {"type": "heading", "attrs": {"level": 2}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Keep operation and presentation separate"}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "A domain Widget owns principal scope, forms, mutations and operation state. A Website Builder Widget owns editable presentation and slots. The domain Widget reads its exact saved relation to Website Builder, then uses that relation's default renderer to render the linked record and forward children. Choosing a frame by title or the first matching variant would connect a different saved instance after an editor adds another frame."}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Relations keep their own identity, ordering and references. They should not choose a business screen or create a checkout form. Module direction also applies to types and frontend imports: Blog can use Website Builder, while an author composition involving Social belongs to a higher consumer. A slot lets the lower presentation accept the resulting content without importing its owner."}]}, {"type": "heading", "attrs": {"level": 2}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Review the actual page"}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Use a saved article with a cover, localized body and ordered Widget associations. Confirm that the page contains those exact records after the visual change. Check loading and error states at the reader, then check one loaded model independently of the grid Widget that repeats it. Test both locales and a built Host route: a browser-created session on a cached page can require a client reader even when the public article remains server-rendered. The component contract and the Article overview source show where each responsibility belongs."}]}, {"type": "heading", "attrs": {"level": 2}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Keep route inputs local"}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Host's leaf Page composition reads named URL segment values inside its render-reader callback. Pass the selected Article slug directly to the Blog consumer. Threading the entire route map through Widgets and relations makes unrelated components depend on page routing and obscures which resource a reader actually requests."}]}, {"type": "heading", "attrs": {"level": 2}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Source code"}]}, {"type": "bulletList", "content": [{"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": ".agents/contracts/engineering/frontend-components.md", "marks": [{"type": "link", "attrs": {"href": "https://github.com/singlepagestartup/singlepagestartup/blob/main/.agents/contracts/engineering/frontend-components.md", "target": "_blank", "rel": "noopener noreferrer"}}]}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "libs/modules/blog/models/article/frontend/component/src/lib/singlepage/default/index.tsx", "marks": [{"type": "link", "attrs": {"href": "https://github.com/singlepagestartup/singlepagestartup/blob/main/libs/modules/blog/models/article/frontend/component/src/lib/singlepage/default/index.tsx", "target": "_blank", "rel": "noopener noreferrer"}}]}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "libs/modules/blog/models/article/frontend/component/src/lib/singlepage/overview-default/Component.tsx", "marks": [{"type": "link", "attrs": {"href": "https://github.com/singlepagestartup/singlepagestartup/blob/main/libs/modules/blog/models/article/frontend/component/src/lib/singlepage/overview-default/Component.tsx", "target": "_blank", "rel": "noopener noreferrer"}}]}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "libs/modules/blog/relations/articles-to-website-builder-module-widgets/frontend/component/src/lib/singlepage/default/Component.tsx", "marks": [{"type": "link", "attrs": {"href": "https://github.com/singlepagestartup/singlepagestartup/blob/main/libs/modules/blog/relations/articles-to-website-builder-module-widgets/frontend/component/src/lib/singlepage/default/Component.tsx", "target": "_blank", "rel": "noopener noreferrer"}}]}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": ".agents/contracts/engineering/module-dependencies.md", "marks": [{"type": "link", "attrs": {"href": "https://github.com/singlepagestartup/singlepagestartup/blob/main/.agents/contracts/engineering/module-dependencies.md", "target": "_blank", "rel": "noopener noreferrer"}}]}]}]}]}]}

description.ru:
{"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "У статьи Blog в SinglePageStartup есть несколько разных ролей: запись базы данных, результат SDK, выбранный frontend-вариант и элемент сохранённой композиции страницы. Явные границы между ними упрощают проверку нового визуала. Карточка может получить другую сетку и типографику, сохранив ID статьи, переводы, связанные файлы и доступные операции. Поэтому изменение страницы начинается с компонента владельца Blog и его reader, а не с дополнительного запроса внутри разметки."}]}, {"type": "heading", "attrs": {"level": 2}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Проследите путь сохранённой записи"}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Обычную схему SPS показывает default-вариант Article. Его index.tsx связывает клиентский SDK Blog, серверный SDK, Provider, компонент загрузки и представление через общий default-компонент. Файл Component.tsx получает загруженную запись и рисует её. У чтения данных остаётся один владелец. Дополнительный fetch в визуальном компоненте создал бы отдельный запрос, собственное ожидание и ещё одно место обработки ошибки для той же статьи."}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Публичный discriminator объявляется в interface.ts. Его точное строковое значение должно присутствовать в действующем variants registry и объединении props. Одного каталога с JSX недостаточно: сохранённое значение variant должно действительно выбирать реализацию. Корневой registry объединяет singlepage и startup. Если проектный override меняет обязательные props, вместе с реализацией обновляется публичный контракт. Иначе вызывающий компонент получает типы одной версии и поведение другой."}]}, {"type": "heading", "attrs": {"level": 2}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Выберите сторону выполнения"}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Server Components и Client Components в Next.js выполняют разные задачи. "}, {"type": "text", "text": "Документация Next.js 15", "marks": [{"type": "link", "attrs": {"href": "https://nextjs.org/docs/15/app/getting-started/server-and-client-components", "target": "_blank", "rel": "noopener noreferrer nofollow"}}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " описывает сериализуемые props и передачу готового содержимого через children. В шаблоне SPS index.tsx выбирает способ чтения, reader получает данные, а интерактивный ClientComponent хранит hooks и браузерное состояние. Параметр isServer выбирает поведение reader SPS; корректная граница клиентского JSX по-прежнему требует соответствующего клиентского entrypoint."}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Для обычного представления сохранённой записи подходит общий reader. Отдельная операция SDK может потребовать локальные client.tsx и server.tsx. Оба reader передают в Component.tsx один типизированный результат. Они заменяют нужную часть чтения, сохраняя устройство варианта. Если обернуть неизменённый общий reader ещё одним Provider, владельцев запроса станет два. Название операции, параметры и результат должны читаться из публичного интерфейса, чтобы ревьюер мог сопоставить их с отображаемыми данными."}]}, {"type": "heading", "attrs": {"level": 2}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Передавайте уже загруженную запись"}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Когда родитель уже располагает актуальным результатом SDK, режим dataSource="props" позволяет дочернему компоненту отобразить запись без нового запроса. Родитель сохраняет подписку, загрузку и обработку ошибок. После refetch он передаёт обновлённые props. Постоянная query-функция, возвращающая старую запись, лишает компонент возможности получить новые данные при согласовании кэша."}]}, {"type": "codeBlock", "attrs": {"language": "tsx"}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "<Article
  variant="overview-default"
  isServer={props.isServer}
  dataSource="props"
  data={props.data}
  language={props.language}
>
  {props.children}
</Article>"}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Так устроен wrapper просмотра статьи Blog. На границе server-to-client выбирайте только публичные UI-параметры, которые нужны дочернему компоненту. Широкий spread props может протащить из reader SDK, Provider или конструкторы компонентов. Приведение TypeScript не превращает эти значения в сериализуемые данные. Серверный render callback вычисляется на сервере; в клиентский слот передаётся готовый React node, который клиент просто отображает."}]}, {"type": "heading", "attrs": {"level": 2}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Разделите операцию и представление"}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Доменный Widget отвечает за текущего пользователя, ограничения доступа, формы, mutations и состояние операции. Widget Website Builder отвечает за редактируемую композицию и слоты. Доменный Widget читает свою точную сохранённую связь с Website Builder и использует default-renderer этой связи. Renderer загружает связанный экземпляр и передаёт ему children. Поиск рамки по заголовку или выбор первого подходящего variant привязал бы операцию к другой записи после появления ещё одной похожей рамки."}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "У связи остаются собственные ID, порядок и ссылки. Relation-компонент не выбирает бизнес-экран и не создаёт форму оплаты. Направление зависимостей действует также для типов и frontend-imports. Blog использует Website Builder, а композиция авторства с Social размещается у более высокого потребителя. Нижний компонент принимает готовое содержимое через слот, не импортируя владельца операции и не меняя порядок модулей ради одного экрана."}]}, {"type": "heading", "attrs": {"level": 2}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Проверьте сохранённую страницу"}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Возьмите статью с обложкой, переводами и несколькими упорядоченными Widget-связями. После изменения визуала страница должна отображать именно эти записи. Отдельно проверьте skeleton и ошибку reader, затем единичную модель и Widget, который повторяет модели в сетке. Переключите язык и откройте собранный Host: браузерная сессия на кэшируемой странице может требовать клиентского reader, пока публичная статья остаётся серверной. Сопоставьте сетевые запросы до и после изменения: повторного чтения того же ID только ради нового представления быть не должно. Контракт компонентов и исходники Article overview дают конкретные точки проверки для каждого из этих условий."}]}, {"type": "heading", "attrs": {"level": 2}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Оставьте параметры маршрута в leaf composition"}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Leaf-композиция Page в Host читает именованные URL segment values внутри callback своего render-reader. Из этой карты выбирается конкретный slug Article и напрямую передаётся потребителю Blog. Полная карта не проходит через Widget и relation props. Иначе промежуточные компоненты начинают зависеть от маршрутизации страницы, хотя им нужен только ID или slug одного ресурса. При проверке откройте две статьи последовательно и сравните параметры SDK: каждый переход должен менять нужный slug, сохраняя остальные публичные props и порядок сохранённых связей."}]}, {"type": "heading", "attrs": {"level": 2}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Исходный код"}]}, {"type": "bulletList", "content": [{"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": ".agents/contracts/engineering/frontend-components.md", "marks": [{"type": "link", "attrs": {"href": "https://github.com/singlepagestartup/singlepagestartup/blob/main/.agents/contracts/engineering/frontend-components.md", "target": "_blank", "rel": "noopener noreferrer"}}]}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "libs/modules/blog/models/article/frontend/component/src/lib/singlepage/default/index.tsx", "marks": [{"type": "link", "attrs": {"href": "https://github.com/singlepagestartup/singlepagestartup/blob/main/libs/modules/blog/models/article/frontend/component/src/lib/singlepage/default/index.tsx", "target": "_blank", "rel": "noopener noreferrer"}}]}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "libs/modules/blog/models/article/frontend/component/src/lib/singlepage/overview-default/Component.tsx", "marks": [{"type": "link", "attrs": {"href": "https://github.com/singlepagestartup/singlepagestartup/blob/main/libs/modules/blog/models/article/frontend/component/src/lib/singlepage/overview-default/Component.tsx", "target": "_blank", "rel": "noopener noreferrer"}}]}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "libs/modules/blog/relations/articles-to-website-builder-module-widgets/frontend/component/src/lib/singlepage/default/Component.tsx", "marks": [{"type": "link", "attrs": {"href": "https://github.com/singlepagestartup/singlepagestartup/blob/main/libs/modules/blog/relations/articles-to-website-builder-module-widgets/frontend/component/src/lib/singlepage/default/Component.tsx", "target": "_blank", "rel": "noopener noreferrer"}}]}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": ".agents/contracts/engineering/module-dependencies.md", "marks": [{"type": "link", "attrs": {"href": "https://github.com/singlepagestartup/singlepagestartup/blob/main/.agents/contracts/engineering/module-dependencies.md", "target": "_blank", "rel": "noopener noreferrer"}}]}]}]}]}]}

description.en:
{"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "A cart quantity can change through a local button, another browser or a backend service. The SPS frontend needs one current SDK result despite those different writers. React Query owns entity results. The action store records requests and revalidation diagnostics. A component's temporary selection and pending state remain with that component. Keeping these owners distinct prevents an event snapshot from becoming an accidental database replica in the browser."}]}, {"type": "heading", "attrs": {"level": 2}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Describe the complete query"}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Factory find, findById and count operations use consistencyQueryKey with the route, parameters and API host. The resulting partition also separates authenticated principals without putting raw credentials in the key. A page filter, offset or different API origin describes different data. Hand-written operations should use the same helper instead of an abbreviated key that can reuse another request's result."}]}, {"type": "codeBlock", "attrs": {"language": "ts"}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "import { consistencyQueryKey } from
  "@sps/shared-frontend-client-api";

const key = consistencyQueryKey(
  "/api/blog/articles",
  { filters: { and: [
    { column: "slug", method: "eq", value: articleSlug }
  ] } },
  clientHost,
);"}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The variables in this example come from the owning reader. The "}, {"type": "text", "text": "TanStack Query key guide", "marks": [{"type": "link", "attrs": {"href": "https://tanstack.com/query/v5/docs/framework/react/guides/query-keys", "target": "_blank", "rel": "noopener noreferrer nofollow"}}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " explains why inputs that change requested data belong in its key. SPS adds the host and principal rules because the same model route can be read against different accounts and servers."}]}, {"type": "heading", "attrs": {"level": 2}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Apply mutations without inventing membership"}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The shared mutation factory handles cache changes before the consumer's onSuccess callback. Create deduplicates by ID and reconciles count; update patches existing detail and list records; delete removes matching records and reconciles count. Hand-written SDK mutations use the same shared helpers and retain action tracking. A toast callback must not replace that internal work."}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "A filtered or paginated list needs membership reasoning. A newly created Article may not belong in the current category, sort position or page. The append helper limits direct insertion to lists whose membership it can establish and uses reconciliation for unknown membership. Patch and remove keep untouched row references. That allows memoized rows with stable ID keys to retain their props when another row changes."}]}, {"type": "heading", "attrs": {"level": 2}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Reconcile other writers"}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Host owns the shared WebSocket connection. Successful API responses can attach an opaque consistency reference to the matching query. The server derives its dependencies from actual reads, including empty relations and count requests. Accepted references receive addressed invalidation and replay. Queries without that coverage keep their established legacy subscription and topic metadata."}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Use the shared subscription lifecycle and return its cleanup from an effect. Creating a socket for every card multiplies connection ownership; adding a periodic entity timer creates another refresh path. The transport contract already defines reconnect behavior, leases and a fallback version check. Incoming invalidations coalesce while a request is running, so a late initial response cannot consume the refresh that arrived during it."}]}, {"type": "heading", "attrs": {"level": 2}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Treat account changes as data changes"}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "A different principal resets private query data, subscriptions and the realtime cursor. A refreshed JWT for the same principal can retain mounted data while queries reconcile. A 401 or 403 reconciliation clears loaded private content. These are data-lifetime rules, not only navigation rules: hiding a section while its protected result stays reachable in a shared cache leaves the old data available to other mounted readers."}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Protected Article content uses QueryScopeProvider with the existing QueryClient. The scope contains a non-secret resource key and a unique mounted-instance owner. Descendant factory queries inherit that scope and use gcTime zero. Disposal cancels and removes only that scope's entries. Public lists and another open protected block retain their own cache and observers. The server remains responsible for permission checks on every protected read."}]}, {"type": "heading", "attrs": {"level": 2}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Verify the lifecycle"}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The article reader derives a deadline from server-checked access and discards protected results when it expires, then asks the canonical operation again. File Storage has a separate protected-byte lifetime. Test those transitions with two subjects and two mounted scopes: a refresh or unmount of one block must not erase another block's public data. Use per-item pending IDs for mutations and stable callbacks for row actions. Keep form subscriptions at the lowest component that needs them. Finally reload the page: the sessionStorage action snapshot is diagnostic and is never restored as entity data or persistent UI state."}]}, {"type": "heading", "attrs": {"level": 2}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Preserve scope ownership"}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Caller query options must not replace a protected scope's key or ownership metadata. A generic cache removal by model route is too broad when two protected sections use that model. Test closing one section while the other is fetching, then remount the first: cancellation from the disposed instance must not remove the replacement instance's active query."}]}, {"type": "heading", "attrs": {"level": 2}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Source code"}]}, {"type": "bulletList", "content": [{"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "libs/shared/frontend/client/api/README.md", "marks": [{"type": "link", "attrs": {"href": "https://github.com/singlepagestartup/singlepagestartup/blob/main/libs/shared/frontend/client/api/README.md", "target": "_blank", "rel": "noopener noreferrer"}}]}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "libs/shared/frontend/client/store/README.md", "marks": [{"type": "link", "attrs": {"href": "https://github.com/singlepagestartup/singlepagestartup/blob/main/libs/shared/frontend/client/store/README.md", "target": "_blank", "rel": "noopener noreferrer"}}]}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "libs/middlewares/src/lib/revalidation/README.md", "marks": [{"type": "link", "attrs": {"href": "https://github.com/singlepagestartup/singlepagestartup/blob/main/libs/middlewares/src/lib/revalidation/README.md", "target": "_blank", "rel": "noopener noreferrer"}}]}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "libs/modules/rbac/models/subject/frontend/component/src/lib/singlepage/me/blog-module/article/private-content-default/client.tsx", "marks": [{"type": "link", "attrs": {"href": "https://github.com/singlepagestartup/singlepagestartup/tree/main/libs/modules/rbac/models/subject/frontend/component/src/lib/singlepage/me/blog-module/article/private-content-default", "target": "_blank", "rel": "noopener noreferrer"}}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " (directory; file is currently in the local branch)"}]}]}, {"type": "listItem", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "libs/modules/rbac/models/subject/frontend/component/src/lib/singlepage/me/blog-module/article/private-content-default/ClientComponent.tsx", "marks": [{"type": "link", "attrs": {"href": "https://github.com/singlepagestartup/singlepagestartup/blob/main/libs/modules/rbac/models/subject/frontend/component/src/lib/singlepage/me/blog-module/article/private-content-default/ClientComponent.tsx", "target": "_blank", "rel": "noopener noreferrer"}}]}]}]}]}]}

